From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cros-disks: read-only disk mounts are read-only, and unmount
 without crashing

Two faults with disks mounted through a FUSE program (NTFS's ntfs-3g):

- A read-only mount was read-only only at the kernel's FUSE mount: the
  program's options never said so, and ntfs-3g opened the device for
  writing and wrote to it (the volume's dirty flag), on a volume mounted
  read-only to keep it unchanged. The program now gets "ro" too. (A
  hibernated Windows volume came up read-only only because ntfs-3g falls
  back to that by itself.)
- MountPoint::Unmount() asks the program of every read-only FUSE mount to
  end its PID namespace, so umount() does not block; the disk mounters
  start theirs without one, and KillPidNamespace() DCHECKs it was asked
  for. With DCHECKs on (test images), unmounting a read-only NTFS volume
  crashed cros-disks, and its restart dropped every other mount.
  KillPidNamespace() now does nothing for such a program, as it in effect
  did without DCHECKs.

diff -ruN a/cros-disks/disk_manager.cc b/cros-disks/disk_manager.cc
--- a/cros-disks/disk_manager.cc
+++ b/cros-disks/disk_manager.cc
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
   std::unique_ptr<SandboxedProcess> PrepareSandbox(
       const std::string& source,
       const base::FilePath&,
-      std::vector<std::string>,
+      std::vector<std::string> params,
       MountError* error) const override {
     auto device = base::FilePath(source);
 
@@ -133,9 +133,18 @@
       return nullptr;
     }
 
-    if (!options_.empty()) {
+    // NickelOS: a read-only mount is read-only for the filesystem's own
+    // program too. Only the kernel's FUSE mount was made read-only, and
+    // ntfs-3g still opened the device for writing and wrote to it (the
+    // volume's dirty flag), also on a volume mounted read-only to keep it
+    // unchanged.
+    std::vector<std::string> program_options = options_;
+    if (IsReadOnlyMount(params)) {
+      program_options.push_back("ro");
+    }
+    if (!program_options.empty()) {
       std::string options;
-      if (!JoinParamsIntoOptions(options_, &options)) {
+      if (!JoinParamsIntoOptions(program_options, &options)) {
         *error = MountError::kInvalidMountOptions;
         return nullptr;
       }
diff -ruN a/cros-disks/sandboxed_process.cc b/cros-disks/sandboxed_process.cc
--- a/cros-disks/sandboxed_process.cc
+++ b/cros-disks/sandboxed_process.cc
@@ -286,7 +286,14 @@
     return false;
   }
 
-  DCHECK(kill_pid_namespace_);
+  // NickelOS: MountPoint::Unmount() asks every read-only FUSE mount's
+  // process to end, also those started without a PID namespace to end (the
+  // NTFS, exFAT and other disk mounters), whose init does not watch the
+  // termination pipe: unmounting a read-only NTFS volume failed this
+  // DCHECK and crashed cros-disks, taking the other mounts with it.
+  if (!kill_pid_namespace_) {
+    return false;
+  }
 
   // Closing termination_fd_ will eventually cause the termination of the 'init'
   // process of the PID namespace.
